<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Möngke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1209">1209</a>–<a href="/years/1259">1259</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Great Khan Möngke, Möngke Khan · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borjigin">Borjigin</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mongke was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> from 1251 to 1259, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>. He sent his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>, leading to the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, and his brother Kublai against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>. He died during a campaign against the Song Dynasty in 1259, triggering a succession struggle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongke.jpg" alt="Möngke" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1438 artist, Shiraz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%B6ngke_enthroned._Tarikh-i_Jahangushay-i_Juvaini,_1438,_Shiraz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Smbat's embassy to Karakorum brought back in 1250 a guarantee of Cilicia's integrity; Het'um I visited <b>Möngke Khan</b> in 1253 and fought under Hulagu at Aleppo and Damascus in 1259–1260, where Arab historians charge his troops with a massacre and arson in the main mosque.</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenian-kingdom-of-cilicia">Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1253 the <b>Great Khan Möngke</b>, Hulagu's brother, ordered him to subdue the remaining Muslim powers of western Asia, assembling one of the largest Mongol armies ever fielded.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After the death of the <b>Great Khan Möngke</b> in 1259, the succession war between Kublai and Ariq Böke and conflicts between the Golden Horde and the Ilkhanate broke the empire into independent khanates pursuing separate policies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>War with the Mongols began in 1235 under the Great Khan Ögedei and continued under <b>Möngke</b>, who died while campaigning in Sichuan in 1259, and finally Kublai Khan, requiring more than four decades to conquer a dynasty that defended itself with fortified cities, river fleets and the deep…</blockquote><a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>…left the Empire with two absentee kings during what historians call the Great Interregnum; and after the death of the <b>Great Khan Möngke</b> in 1259 rival kurultais elected his brothers Kublai Khan and Ariq Böke, whose war, the Toluid Civil War, hastened the division of the Mongol Empire.</blockquote><a href="/government/elective-monarchy">Elective monarchy · Weaknesses</a></li><li><blockquote>The deaths of Ögedei in 1241 and <b>Möngke</b> in 1259 called princes home to choose a successor, and in 1260 rival kurultais elected Kublai Khan and his brother Ariq Böke.</blockquote><a href="/government/nomadic-confederation">Nomadic confederation · Through History</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>. Died in Diaoyu Fortress, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=30.01,106.31&amp;year=1241" aria-label="Diaoyu Fortress on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7312 1068 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Möngke"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7762 1338h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7762 1338h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=30.01,106.31&amp;year=1241">What was here in 1241? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
